    "result_text": "All **70 tests pass** with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity. The V2 version tag is mixed **only inside the identifiers**, and the response/audit shapes were restructured.\n\n**Identity derivation \u2014 rederived with a fixed `V2` tag (every identifier changes, no V1 value recurs):**\n- `Localities.java` \u2014 added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and `identityRegion(city, postcode)` = `\"V2\" + region(...)` (e.g. `V2NSW`), the region code used inside the identifiers. Decoupled the user-facing `region(Owner)` (locality) to derive the **plain** region straight from city/postcode, so the tag never leaks into `locality`/`timezone`/segment; removed the now-unused `regionOfCode`.\n- `AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 memberId prefix now uses `identityRegion` \u2192 `V2NSW26\u2026`.\n- `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 householdId hashes `\"V2\" + \"|\" + lastName + \"|\" + postcode` (same lastName+postcode still share it).\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 identityKey hashes `\"V2\" + \"|\" + telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex` (still 64-hex SHA-256).\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; added a nested `OwnerIdentity` schema (those three) as `identity`, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` + new `OwnerIdentities.java` helper \u2014 maps `identity` (grouped) and `apiVersion: 2`.\n\n**Audit schema v2:**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` \u2014 added `schemaVersion` (`SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`) and a recomputed `ownerSegment` (via `OwnerSegments.of`, whose region stays plain).\n\n**Unchanged:** request fields (`OwnerFields`), and `locality`/`timezone`/segment remain the plain region code \u2014 verified by Cp17/Cp30/Cp42/Cp55 passing alongside the V2 tests (Cp11/28/32/36/52/53/56/60).",
