    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here is the ordered account of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 403/401.\n\nThe pipeline then runs these steps in order, all inside a single `transaction` that commits at the end:\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotency`\n- **Side-effect:** republishes the `Idempotency-Key` header (may be null) as a variable for later recording.\n- **Short-circuit (not a rejection):** if the key was already used *and* its owner still exists, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 replays the original owner with **200**, skipping the rest of the pipeline (in particular, ahead of the duplicate check that would otherwise 409 the repeat).\n\n## 2. `ValidateOwnerFields` (the body-binding/validation step) \u2014 all failures collect into one 400 (`MissingFieldsException`)\n- **Validation:** `firstName` required (non-blank).\n- **Validation:** `lastName` required.\n- **Validation:** address required \u2014 accepts either structured (`addressLine1` + optional `addressLine2`) or flat `address`; structured preferred when `addressLine1` non-blank; **side-effect:** normalizes the supplied form and republishes a composed, normalized `address` (and normalized line1/line2).\n- **Validation:** `city` required.\n- **Validation:** `telephone` required and must normalize to valid E.164; **side-effect:** republishes the normalized E.164 telephone.\n- **Validation (conditional):** `email` only if present \u2014 must pass syntactic regex and must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); **side-effect:** normalized to trimmed lower-case and republished.\n- **Validation (conditional):** `postcode` only if present \u2014 must be exactly 4 digits and within the city's region range (`NSW 2000\u20132099`, `VIC 3000\u20133099`, `QLD 4000\u20134099`; unknown region accepts any 4-digit); **side-effect:** republishes the trimmed postcode.\n- **Validation (conditional):** `registrationDate` only if present \u2014 must not be later than the server's current date.\n- **Side-effect:** republishes the validated/normalized `OwnerFieldsDto` for downstream steps.\n\n## 3. `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** rejects with 409 (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (city compared case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed).\n\n## 4. `EnsureDailyLimit`\n- **Validation:** rejects with 429 (`DailyLimitException`) if \u2265 100 owners already have today's business-day-adjusted registration date.\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied or today's `LocalDate.now()`), then **business-day-adjusts it** (weekends roll forward to Monday).\n\n## 6. `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** if a postcode is present, sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`. No postcode \u2192 no household (null).\n\n## 7. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- **Validation:** the consolidated duplicate check \u2014 rejects with 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException`) if the owner's `identityKey` (SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`) exactly matches any existing **non-deleted** owner. Soft-deleted owners are ignored.\n\n## 8. `AssignHouseholdSize`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus 1 (this new owner). No household \u2192 1.\n\n## 9. `AssignMemberId`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode/city with V2 tag, 2-digit fiscal year, 8 hex of SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`, Luhn check digit); on collision with an existing `memberId`, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to make it unique.\n\n## 10. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## 11. `AssignMembershipLevel`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `membershipLevel` from `MembershipLevels.of(owner)`, but **capped** at one above the maximum level among existing (non-deleted) household members (valued at the new household size). No existing member \u2192 uncapped.\n\n## 12. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already registered today (business-day-adjusted).\n\n## 13. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** soft-match flag. If `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`. Otherwise, if the owner has a postcode and some existing non-deleted owner shares `soundex(lastName)` + equal postcode but a *different* identityKey, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id (lowest id wins). Else false/null.\n\n## 14. `AssignCapacityWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `capacityWarning` = true if the city currently holds 40\u201349 owners (inclusive).\n\n## 15. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner (`repository.save`), generating its id.\n\n## 16. `RecordIdempotency`\n- **Side-effect:** if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the idempotency store (no-op otherwise).\n\n## 17. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** logs a human-readable audit line (`AUDIT` logger) with id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n## 18. `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent`\n- **Side-effect:** logs a structured JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (`AUDIT` logger) with a process-wide monotonic `seq`.\n\n## 19. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`\n- **Side-effect:** logs a welcome line on the `NOTIFY` logger with id and memberId.\n\n## 20. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Summary of the rejection points, in order:** 403/401 (role) \u2192 200 replay (idempotent repeat) \u2192 400 (field validation, batched) \u2192 409 (city at capacity) \u2192 429 (daily limit) \u2192 409 (duplicate identity). Everything after the duplicate check is pure assignment/persistence/audit side-effects \u2014 no further rejections.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging while reading: the `city`-capacity, daily-limit, household, namesake, member-id, and possible-duplicate steps each independently call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and scan in memory (O(n) per step, so ~a dozen full-table scans per create), and several counting steps (`EnsureDailyLimit`, `AssignBulkSignupWarning`, capacity) don't exclude soft-deleted owners the way the duplicate checks do \u2014 I'm only describing current behavior as asked, not changing anything."
